  from environment variables.
- Apply this model selection logic as a single shared utility function 
  (e.g. `get_model_for_playbook(playbook_name: str) -> str`) and use it 
  everywhere LLM calls are made.

## Constraints
- Do not break any existing functionality.
- Do not change API contracts or response schemas.
- Do not add new dependencies.
- Keep changes production-grade: proper error handling, logging, no silent 
  failures on the capabilities/decomposition steps.
- If capabilities or decomposition generation fails, log the error clearly 
  and return an empty list/dict rather than null, so the frontend degrades 
  gracefully.

## Steps to follow
1. Find all places where `capabilities` and `decomposition` are set in the 
   response — trace from the API handler back to the agent/LLM call.
2. Find all LLM model instantiation points in the codebase.
3. Replace every hardcoded model string with the env-var-based utility 
